              "blocks": {
                "text_wzPLEx": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Collagen is the most abundant protein in your body. It makes up about 30% of all your protein. Think of it as the structure that holds your skin together — it gives skin its firmness, bounce, and smoothness. After about 25, your body produces less collagen every year. That's when fine lines, sagging, and dryness start to appear. No cream can replace collagen from the outside. It has to come from within.</p>",
